  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want Réglages › Sécurité to drop the sentence under « Verrouiller l'app (Face ID / code) ». What the switch does is obvious, and the section is shorter without it. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17.)\n\n### Today (dev-swift)\n\n`App/SwiftHFR/Settings/SecuritySettingsSections.swift:42-43`, the « Sécurité » section footer: « L'app se verrouille au lancement et au retour après le délai choisi ; le code de l'appareil remplace Face ID. » (LOT-173).\n\n### Scope\n\n- Remove that footer. The switch, the « Verrouiller » delay picker and the error or status message (`lock.message`, `:36-37`) stay.\n- If LOT-173's spec (`docs/lots/LOT-173-keychain-sync-lock.md`) quotes the footer, update it.\n- **Grouped with #1065** (same file, same agent, same PR).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- The section has no footer.\n- The lock tests stay green.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nRéglages › Sécurité: no sentence under the switch.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
